            At matching tiers these two brands are far closer than the shelf suggests — both are asphalt emulsions, both last two to three years, and both live or die on how thickly they went down. <strong class="text-white">Compare tier to tier, not badge to badge.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Latex-ite for textured or sloped drives; Henry for large flat ones and first-time applicators.</strong> Then spend your effort where it actually pays: clean the surface, fill the cracks, and put down two thin coats instead of one thick one.
          </p>
